<title>USA: Iraqi oil sale still on 'strong hold'- US official.</title>
<headline>Iraqi oil sale still on 'strong hold'- US official.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iraq's oil-for-food deal with the United Nations is not likely to be implemented imminently, a well-placed Clinton administration official said Wednesday.</p>
<p>His comments were in contrast to remarks by U.N. officials in the last few days suggesting that oil-for-food sales could be back on track shortly.</p>
<p>&quot;I think that's still on sort of a 'strong hold,'&quot; the U.S. official said. &quot;I'm unaware of any strong pressure coming from any quarter saying let's get along with this.&quot;</p>
</text>
